  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through Monday)\nIssued at 345 AM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nIn the extended, the upper ridge is still forecast to meander west \ninto next week, with the LREF and global models in agreement in \ntaking it southwest of the Four Corners by Friday morning.  This \nwill precipitate a decrease in thicknesses a little, offering some \n(but not much) relief from the warm weather of the past few days, \neven if KMAF's peak climatological annual heating is only a couple \nof days away.  Heat Advisories may still be needed to some extent or \nanother each day beginning around Friday or so.  Toward the weekend, \nthe ridge may be far enough west that isolated convection may creep \nback into the mix, mainly Southeast New Mexico and the higher \nterrain of West Texas.  Models try to bring a very weak cold front \ninto the area Saturday, which may kick off a little convection\nSaturday evening. But rain chances will be minimal at best.",
